8. Intellectual Structure and Categorization Protection

The EFU Project includes a unique and original intellectual structure consisting of:

- A system of approximately 70 base emojis (categories)
- A defined mapping where each base emoji is associated with a set of related emojis
- A two-step selection model designed for fast and intuitive emoji access

This structure, including its organization, grouping logic, and selection methodology,
constitutes an original intellectual design created by the author.

This structure is made freely available for NON-COMMERCIAL use.

However, the following are strictly prohibited without prior written authorization:

- Commercial use of the EFU categorization model
- Reproduction of the same or substantially similar emoji grouping system
- Use of identical or equivalent base-to-emoji mappings in commercial software
- Integration of this structure into paid or monetized applications

Any system that reproduces or closely mimics the EFU structure,
even if implemented with different code, will be considered a derivative work.

Commercial use of this structure requires a formal licensing agreement.

